# Cloudflare reads this file from `out/` (Next copies `public/` as is) and does
# NOT serve it as an asset, same as `_redirects`.
#
# WHY: the same build answers on three hosts, and only one of them is the site.
#   - sevenz.site                              <- the site
#   - sevenz-web.sevenz-mvp.workers.dev        <- `npx wrangler deploy`, used to check a deploy
#   - sevenz-site.sevenz-mvp.workers.dev       <- the git-built worker that serves the domain,
#     plus its preview aliases (`dev-sevenz-site...`, `<hash>-sevenz-site...`)
# All of them returned 200 with `index, follow` on 2026-11-15. The canonical
# already points at sevenz.site, but a canonical is a hint Google may ignore;
# this header is an instruction. Without it the workers.dev copies can compete
# with the domain for the same query, which is the opposite of what we want
# while the domain is still being indexed for the first time.
#
# The URLs keep working: the deploy checks in dashboard/CLAUDE.md still read
# them. They only stop being eligible for search results.
#
# Pattern taken from Cloudflare's own docs ("Prevent your workers.dev URLs
# showing in search results"), checked 2026-11-15. A placeholder stops at a
# period, so it takes two of them to cover `<worker>.<account>.workers.dev`.
# The rule matches on host only; sevenz.site never receives this header.
https://:worker.:account.workers.dev/*
  X-Robots-Tag: noindex
